# The pass that films: Anima Song plus PickleTools' film steps, and nothing else.
#
# Select it with -DepMap wsl-deps.film.map. The film scenario is @wip, so it is skipped in every pass that
# does not stage the steps it needs; play it with -pickle-include-wip AND a filter, which the launcher requires:
#
#   powershell.exe -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/Run-PickleWsl.ps1 -Mod AnimaSong `
#       -DepMap wsl-deps.film.map -IncludeWip -Filter '::filmed one picture per tick'
#
# nelim.pickletools.filmticks is a folder of this repository, not a Workshop item: the staging reads a
# `path:` line as a folder relative to the repository root. It is test infrastructure, not an optional
# integration of the mod, which is why it lives in its own map and not in wsl-deps.map (there is none: the
# staging reads that name on every pass, and a suite owning one can never have a pass without it).
nelim.pickletools.filmticks   path:PickleTools/FilmTicks/Mod
